{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774749,"nonce":"19RY/t7ECPEhS+UJK/Qm0lTGAbw=","title":"The warm space bound: budget, real LRU, classed eviction (cba7165)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #105 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/cba7165-warm-bound` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-08-26T12:38:07Z · Merged: 2026-08-26T13:11:14Z\n\nThe warm tier gets a landlord (git-bug `cba7165`) — **stacked on #102** (merge that first). **922/922 green.** Full chain: design → skeptical audit → independent judge (keystone verified: post-0067, warm eviction can never lose the only copy of durable content) → build → review → fixups.\n\n**What ships:**\n- **A budget**: `SCARAB_WORKSPACE_WARM_BUDGET_BYTES` (default: 90% of the warm mount via statvfs — honest caveat documented: on a shared dev disk that's effectively unbounded, so local-proc sets an explicit 2 GiB). High-water evicts down to 80%, background-only — zero hot-path cost.\n- **A real LRU key**: warm hits coarsely refresh mtime (1h grain, fire-and-forget, off the response path) — fixing the banked 24476bc finding that last-*written* is the wrong key for immutable content read forever.\n- **Classed eviction**: committed-durable first (free — re-fetchable from packs), cache-only second (a licensed miss); a 1h min-age floor plus an unlink-time re-lstat protect in-flight content; only 64-hex-named files directly under `blobs/`/`trees/` are ever touched (staging temps and the readyz probe are structurally spared).\n- **Fail-safe by construction**: classification only *orders* — safety comes from the floor + pack fall-through reads, so even a DB outage degrades to pure LRU rather than either skipping (disk fills) or over-deleting. The rationale is written at the degrade site for the next maintainer.\n- One-shot boot reap of pre-#99 `farms/` leftovers (lstat-guarded); under-budget passes use a count-only walk (no per-file allocation churn at millions of blobs).\n\n**Race tests drive the real production pass between client operations**: mid-stream eviction completes byte-identical off the open handle; evict-then-GET re-serves from the pack and re-warms; a cache-only eviction surfaces as an honest `missing_warm` + 404 (no PR #103 coupling); the unlink-time re-check is compile-load-bearing (the loop cannot build without it).\n\n**Bonus fix, already pushed to #102's branch (`9e09042`):** stacking this branch exposed that #102's intermittent floor-test failure was a real clock-authority bug — `depot_packs.created_at` from the host clock vs the epoch from Postgres `now()` (7/25 repro at the branch tip; boot-adjacent drains would silently defer behind the reachability floor in production). Both INSERTs now stamp from Postgres. 0/25 after.\n\nWith this, the Depot's storage story closes end to end: one-pass durable writes (#95), replica-safe drains (#97), staging reclaim (#100), the borrow ledger (#101), committed expiry + profiles (#102), the warm-only Cache (#103), and a bounded warm tier (this).\n\nCloses `cba7165` on merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}